# DIR - Directory listing

```text
DIR [DU:][filespec]
```

## Resident DIR

Type `DIR` at the command prompt to list files in the current drive and
user area. Supply a drive/user or a wildcard to narrow the listing.

```text
DIR B3:*.ASM
DIR B[-]:*.COM
```

The first command lists assembly sources in B3. The second lists COM
files across the user areas on B.

## Transient DIR

Use `:DIR` to run DIR.COM. To page through a long listing or locate a
particular filename, use:

```text
:DIR /P
:DIR /WHEREIS ED.COM
```

Use `:DIR /H` for the transient command's option summary.
